.temp/spawn-runs/RUN-260731-d6033b/runner.log:11349:{"body":"Six cases on the Windows runner of the Test lane are left after PR 12 and\nPR 13. Five are in `internal/transaction` and one is\n`internal/godriver TestFingerprintReportsUnreadableDirectoryIdentically`.\nThey are three separate facts stated in a syntax only unix hosts speak.\n\n## An owned entry's content is path text in the host's own syntax\n\n`os.Symlink` rewrites its destination through `filepath.FromSlash` on\nWindows, because `/` is not a separator inside a reparse point. The engine\nalready round-trips whatever the host recorded — `os.Readlink` into the\njournal, the journal back into the link — so a rollback there restores\n`..\\old\\skill` exactly, and four cases failed only because they compared it\nwith the literal `../old/skill` they had passed to `os.Symlink`.\n\nThose cases now state their expectation as the destination the host\nactually recorded at creation. That is a stricter comparison than the\nliteral was, not a looser one: it pins the restored link against what was\nreally on disk rather than against what the fixture asked for.\n\n- `TestCommitAndRollbackRestoreALinkExactly`\n- `TestRecoveryFinishesAPreparedLinkTransaction`\n- `TestEntryRemovalRestoresTheExactLink`\n- `TestEntryTargetsDoNotAliasTheirDestination`\n\n## The namespace pass snapshot was not a snapshot on Windows\n\n`TestNamespaceIdentityIsReadOnceWithinOneValidationPass` is a real defect\nrather than a fixture one. `os.Stat` and `os.Lstat` on Windows return a\nrecord that has still to read the volume serial and file index from the\nlive filesystem; `os.SameFile` performs that read the first time it is\nasked. Two things follow for the pairwise independence sweep, and the rest\nof it assumes neither.\n\nThe snapshot did not hold: a path resolved early in a pass had its object\nread at whatever later moment the first surviving pair reached it, so the\nsweep could compare one path as it was against another as it had since\nbecome.\n\nAnd a failed read was fail-open. `os.SameFile` answers only with a bool, so\na read it could not perform — the object replaced or removed under the\npass, a handle the process cannot open — arrived at the sweep as \"these are\ndifferent objects\", which is the answer that lets an aliased pair through.\nThe unix hosts have no such branch: a stat that cannot answer fails there\nand the pair fails closed on it.\n\n`completeNamespaceIdentity` now finishes the read where the identity is\ntaken. Every later comparison is an in-memory one on every platform, and a\nread that cannot be completed becomes the inspection failure the sweep\nalready refuses. `TestWindowsNamespaceIdentityIsCompletedWhenItIsTaken`\npins both halves.\n\n## `os.Chmod` on Windows only toggles the read-only attribute\n\n`TestFingerprintReportsUnreadableDirectoryIdentically` stated an unreadable\ndirectory as mode `0o000`, which leaves a Windows directory perfectly\nlistable, so the walk-error branch it exists to cover never happened. It\nnow goes through `denyDirectoryListing`, which is the mode bits on unix and\na protected DACL denying `FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY` on Windows — the grant\nbeside it propagates to children so the temporary root stays removable, the\ndenial does not.\n\n## Ledger\n\nAll six cases are added to `platform-cases.tsv` with no skip tolerance.\nThis runner set can create a link on all three platforms — `internal/adapters\nTestSymlinkModeStagesRelativeLinkTargets` already requires exactly that of\nit — so the link-capability skip these cases carry firing here would be a\nreal loss of coverage, and the gate should say so.\n\nNo skip, tolerance, platform exclusion or suppression is introduced by this\nchange.\n\nBoard: BUG-260731-38dz6m","comments":[],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T15:32:47Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T15:36:05Z","messageBody":"Six cases on the Windows runner asserted facts that are true only where a\npath is written with forward slashes and where a stat answers with the\nobject it named.\n\nAn owned entry's content is path text in the host's own syntax: os.Symlink\nrewrites its destination through filepath.FromSlash, because '/' is not a\nseparator inside a reparse point. The engine already round-trips whatever\nthe host recorded -- readlink into the journal, journal back into the link\n-- so the four entry cases now state their expectation as the destination\nthe host actually recorded, which makes \"restored exactly\" an exact\ncomparison everywhere instead of a POSIX literal only unix can satisfy.\n\nThe namespace pass snapshot was the real defect. os.Stat and os.Lstat on\nWindows return a record that has still to read the volume serial and file\nindex from the live filesystem, and os.SameFile performs that read at the\ncomparison. The snapshot was therefore not a snapshot -- one path was read\nas it had since become while another was read as it was -- and a read that\ncould not be performed reached the sweep as \"these are different objects\",\nthe answer that lets an aliased pair through. The identity is now completed\nwhere it is taken, so every later comparison is an in-memory one on every\nplatform and an unreadable identity is the inspection failure the sweep\nalready refuses.\n\nThe fingerprint case stated an unreadable directory as mode 0o000, which on\nWindows only toggles the read-only attribute and leaves the directory\nlistable. It now goes through denyDirectoryListing, which is the mode bits\non unix and a protected DACL denying FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY on Windows.\n\nAll six are added to the platform-case ledger without a skip tolerance, so\na link this runner set can create, and a boundary it can impose, are\nrequired rather than assumed.","messageHeadline":"State the Windows half of the entry and namespace contracts","oid":"d07284571f6c6be996e57c09e129cb35d0773c54"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T22:01:54Z","authors":[{"email":"oparin@me.com","id":"U_kgDOBdwbVg","login":"ivanopcode","name":"Ivan Oparin"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-31T22:01:54Z","messageBody":"The hosted Windows runner can bypass a deny ACE when Go opens a directory with backup intent, so the DACL fixture did not make the directory unreadable. Hold a read handle with zero sharing instead: later directory opens fail with a native sharing violation regardless of ACL privileges. Assert the fixture's listing boundary directly before comparing both fingerprint implementations.","messageHeadline":"Make the Windows unreadable fixture privilege-proof","oid":"a134fdc422b2fea3c4c1ac09b1f8f7c4afbc75a2"}],"mergeStateStatus":"UNSTABLE","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","reviewDecision":"","title":"State the Windows half of the entry and namespace contracts"}
.temp/spawn-runs/RUN-260731-d6033b/runner.log:11470:/bin/zsh -lc "task-board m 'set_notes(BUG-260731-38dz6m, text=\"DEVELOPER CHECKPOINT RUN-260731-d6033b: native Windows artifact 8799245786 proved PR15 head d0728457 left only TestFingerprintReportsUnreadableDirectoryIdentically failing because the DACL fixture remained listable. Go 1.25 opens directories with backup intent, so the administrative hosted runner can bypass the deny ACE. Signed fix a134fdc replaces the ACL fixture with a GENERIC_READ directory handle held at zero sharing and asserts os.ReadDir is actually refused. Local exit-0 gates: focused six cases, full godriver+transaction, Windows amd64 cross-compiles, go vet ./..., go build ./..., golangci-lint v2.12.2 (0 issues), go test -count=1 ./.... PR15 CI run 30668611796 is active; Ubuntu Test/Lint and macOS Test are green at checkpoint, Windows Test still executing.\")'" in /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator
.temp/spawn-runs/RUN-260731-d6033b/runner.log:11472:{"ok":true,"result":{"id":"BUG-260731-38dz6m","notes":"Created from RUN-260731-1b588e round-8 evidence. Scheduling dependency is BUG-260731-33v6zz / PR 13 so the residual fix is developed and validated against the combined Windows base and does not collide in internal/godriver. PR 12 is already merged as b30773b8.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: disabled; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=launch_composition_disabled; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260731-997143, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260731-997143)\nSix residuals named from the combined-base windows-latest go-test JSON. internal/transaction: TestCommitAndRollbackRestoreALinkExactly / TestRecoveryFinishesAPreparedLinkTransaction / TestEntryRemovalRestoresTheExactLink / TestEntryTargetsDoNotAliasTheirDestination / TestNamespaceIdentityIsReadOnceWithinOneValidationPass. internal/godriver: TestFingerprintReportsUnreadableDirectoryIdentically. Three causes -- link destinations are host syntax because os.Symlink applies filepath.FromSlash on Windows; the namespace pass snapshot left the Windows file identity deferred to os.SameFile so it was neither a snapshot nor fail-closed; os.Chmod 0o000 leaves a Windows directory listable. PR 15 opened on task/BUG-260731-38dz6m-windows-residuals.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=1)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260731-997143, pid=96578, exit=1)\nDEVELOPER INFRA INTERRUPTION RUN-260731-997143: published signed Curator PR15 head d0728457 and started all-platform CI, then Claude Opus 5 returned HTTP 429 monthly spend limit while waiting for Windows. This is not a developer handoff or verdict. Resume with Opus after capacity returns; inspect CI run 30643616475, complete checklist/evidence, then route to fresh Opus review.\nCI CHECKPOINT 2026-07-31T16:01Z: Curator PR15 run 30643616475 at signed head d0728457 has 11/12 jobs terminal green/skipped as expected: Ubuntu Test/Race, macOS Test/Race, lint, three gate self-tests, interop, naming; only Windows Test remains in progress inside go test since 15:36:43Z (24m at checkpoint). Do not cancel blindly; inspect terminal result/log first when resuming. No Opus verdict exists.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: disabled; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=launch_composition_disabled; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260731-d6033b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260731-d6033b)\nDEVELOPER CHECKPOINT RUN-260731-d6033b: native Windows artifact 8799245786 proved PR15 head d0728457 left only TestFingerprintReportsUnreadableDirectoryIdentically failing because the DACL fixture remained listable. Go 1.25 opens directories with backup intent, so the administrative hosted runner can bypass the deny ACE. Signed fix a134fdc replaces the ACL fixture with a GENERIC_READ directory handle held at zero sharing and asserts os.ReadDir is actually refused. Local exit-0 gates: focused six cases, full godriver+transaction, Windows amd64 cross-compiles, go vet ./..., go build ./..., golangci-lint v2.12.2 (0 issues), go test -count=1 ./.... PR15 CI run 30668611796 is active; Ubuntu Test/Lint and macOS Test are green at checkpoint, Windows Test still executing."}}
