30773b` | head `1160346` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cmd/curator` | 8 fail | **0** (63 pass, 0 skip) |\n| `internal/buildcache` | 1 | **0** (51 pass, 4 pre-existing skips) |\n| `internal/globalbins` | 1 | **0** |\n| `internal/managerlock` | 2 | **0** |\n| `internal/staging` | 1 | **0** |\n\nAll 14 originally-named cases re-checked individually: every one `pass`. Whole-lane residual is exactly 6 (`internal/transaction` ×5, one `godriver` case), already red on `main` and owned by `BUG-260731-38dz6m`.\n\n**No relaxation.** `git diff origin/main -- .github/` is empty; `ledger-consistency: ok` (56 rows). My skip set-diff ran at *every* nesting level: the only skips appearing at head are two `TestCompiledProjectStatusRepairRollbackRecovery` subtests, and the guard producing them (`status_test.go:1100`) is byte-identical to `main:1098` and untouched by the diff — they were unreachable at base because the parent failed first. The 4 skips the branch adds never fired; all 7 new regression tests ran and passed. Zero regressions.\n\n**Unix preservation is structural**, not just empirical: the buildcache changes are `//go:build windows`, `physicalPath` on unix is exactly the `EvalSymlinks` call it replaced, and `runtimestore.Platform()` makes the globalbins change a no-op off Windows. Locally: `go build ./...` and `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` both exit 0.\n\n**Scope:** `install`/`buildsource`/`transaction`/`runtimestore` are byte-unchanged vs `main`. The `internal/godriver` breach I ratified — `BUG-260731-lepevi` is done with PR 11 merged, no file overlap, and the GOROOT directory-junction defect was genuinely unreachable from the owned packages.\n\n**Five non-blocking findings** recorded in `BUG-260731-33v6zz_review-verdict.md`, board notes, and LOGBOOK:\n1. The published results artifact is stale (74-red table predates PR 12); should be refreshed via `update_resource`.\n2. Low-severity residual TOCTOU — `ownedInheritingDirectory` checks via handle, `protectWindowsPath` then re-resolves by path through `SetNamedSecurityInfo`, which follows reparse points. `SetSecurityInfo` on the open handle would close it.\n3. `TestWindowsPublicationRefusesAHomeOwnedByAnotherPrincipal` doesn't test a foreign owner — it tests an explicit non-owner grant on a self-owned home.\n4. `managerlock.identityBelow` spells its expectation through the production function, so the Windows spelling assertion is tautological (mitigated by behavioral case-alias tests).\n5. Only `ensureProtectedBase` repairs the home, so a cold `Inspect` on Windows reports `UntrustedProvenance` rather than a miss until first publication.\n\nPer the reviewer constraint I supplied no `commit_ack` — the acceptance evidence is on the board for the commit-owning mover, which commits the scope and finalizes with `commit_ack=scope_committed`. `LOGBOOK.md` is modified and uncommitted.","ttft_ms":2700,"ttft_stream_ms":2166,"time_to_request_ms":29,"type":"result","duration_ms":681643,"uuid":"e0d81da5-4fdd-46a5-9661-85d8ecb09512"}
