re that exact value after commit, recovery, or rollback:\n\n- `TestCommitAndRollbackRestoreALinkExactly`\n- `TestRecoveryFinishesAPreparedLinkTransaction`\n- `TestEntryRemovalRestoresTheExactLink`\n- `TestEntryTargetsDoNotAliasTheirDestination`\n\n## Eager Windows namespace identity\n\n`TestNamespaceIdentityIsReadOnceWithinOneValidationPass` exposed a product\ndefect. On Windows, the record returned by `os.Stat`/`os.Lstat` still defers the\nvolume serial and file index read until `os.SameFile`. That made a supposed pass\nsnapshot depend on later filesystem state, and a failed deferred read collapsed\nto `false`, which is the fail-open answer \"different objects.\"\n\n`completeNamespaceIdentity` now forces that identity read while the snapshot is\ntaken. Later comparisons are in-memory on every platform, and an identity that\ncannot be completed becomes the inspection failure the namespace sweep already\nrefuses. `TestWindowsNamespaceIdentityIsCompletedWhenItIsTaken` pins both\nproperties.\n\n## Privilege-proof unreadable-directory fixture\n\n`os.Chmod(0o000)` only toggles the read-only attribute on Windows, so it does\nnot make a directory unreadable. The first Windows fixture replaced it with a\ndeny ACE, but native run 30643616475 proved the hosted administrative runner\ncould still list the directory: Go opens directories with backup intent and\n`SeBackupPrivilege` can bypass that DACL.\n\nThe Windows fixture now holds a `GENERIC_READ` directory handle with share mode\nzero. Every later `Open`/`OpenRoot` read fails with a native sharing violation,\nregardless of ACL privileges. The test first asserts that `os.ReadDir` is truly\nrefused, then requires the legacy and scoped fingerprints to report the same\n`toolchain_unreadable` result. Unix keeps the mode-bit fixture.\n\n## Coverage and policy\n\nAll six top-level cases are explicit in `platform-cases.tsv`. No skip,\ntolerance, platform exclusion, ledger relaxation, or broad suppression is\nintroduced.\n\nLocal validation on signed head `a134fdc`:\n\n- focused six-case tests: exit 0\n- full `internal/godriver` + `internal/transaction`: exit 0\n- Windows amd64 test-binary cross-compiles for both packages: exit 0\n- `go vet ./...`: exit 0\n- `go build ./...`: exit 0\n- `golangci-lint v2.12.2`: exit 0, 0 issues\n- `go test -count=1 ./...`: exit 0\n\nNative matrix: https://github.com/relux-works/curator/actions/runs/30668611796/attempts/2\n\n- all required jobs green on signed head `a134fdc`\n- all six named Windows cases pass in artifact `8809078378`\n- no `fail` row exists in the Windows observed-case report\n- the unrelated managerlock case that flaked on attempt 1 passes on attempt 2\n\nBoard: BUG-260731-38dz6m\n","created_at":"2026-07-31T15:36:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T23:07:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"646275fa58b298a12cf7166aab1fa1960a78191d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relux-works/curator/pulls/15/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relux-works/curator/pulls/15/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relux-works/curator/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relux-works/curator/issues/15/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/relux-works/curator/statuses/a134fdc422b2fea3c4c1ac09b1f8f7c4afbc75a2","head":{"label":"relux-works:task/BUG-260731-38dz6m-windows-residuals","ref":"task/BUG-260731-38dz6m-windows-residuals","sha":"a134fdc422b2fea3c4c1ac09b1f8f7c4afbc75a2","user":{"login":"relux-works","id":261817730,"node_id":"O_kgDOD5sFgg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261817730?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/relux-works","html_url":"https://github.com/relux-works","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/relux-works/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/relux-work