    "payload": "tree 94e656c1c7de1e1c1f6463bfc54e7676b418e0d8\nparent d07284571f6c6be996e57c09e129cb35d0773c54\nauthor Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com> 1785535314 +0300\ncommitter Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com> 1785535314 +0300\n\nMake the Windows unreadable fixture privilege-proof\n\nThe hosted Windows runner can bypass a deny ACE when Go opens a directory with backup intent, so the DACL fixture did not make the directory unreadable. Hold a read handle with zero sharing instead: later directory opens fail with a native sharing violation regardless of ACL privileges. Assert the fixture's listing boundary directly before comparing both fingerprint implementations.\n",
